  "text": "Veterinary Chemotherapy | Southern Colorado Veterinary Internal Medicine\nSkip to content\nFacebook\nInstagram\nPhone: 719-272-4004\n|\nfrontdesk@imvets.com\nHome\nAbout Us\nAbout Our Practice\nAbout Internal Medicine\nAbout Veterinary Oncology\nAbout Our Specialists\nChris McReynolds, DVM, DACVIM\nMacon Miles, DVM, DACVIM\nAmelia Keith, DVM, DACVIM\nJennifer Garcia,  DVM, DACVIM\nMegan Kelley, DVM, DACVIM\nCarson Zweck-Bronner, DVM, DACVIM\nKeira Sztukowski, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nEmily Lunger, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nAbout Our Support Veterinarians\nAngela Van House. DVM\nBlake Wood, DVM\nServices\nPet Owners\nLocation & Directions\nAppointments\nFinancial Options\nPrescription Refills\nPet Cancer Resource Center\nPrivacy Policy\nVeterinarians\nCareers\nSearch for:\nHome\nAbout Us\nAbout Our Practice\nAbout Internal Medicine\nAbout Veterinary Oncology\nAbout Our Specialists\nChris McReynolds, DVM, DACVIM\nMacon Miles, DVM, DACVIM\nAmelia Keith, DVM, DACVIM\nJennifer Garcia,  DVM, DACVIM\nMegan Kelley, DVM, DACVIM\nCarson Zweck-Bronner, DVM, DACVIM\nKeira Sztukowski, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nEmily Lunger, DVM, DACVIM (Oncology)\nAbout Our Support Veterinarians\nAngela Van House. DVM\nBlake Wood, DVM\nServices\nPet Owners\nLocation & Directions\nAppointments\nFinancial Options\nPrescription Refills\nPet Cancer Resource Center\nPrivacy Policy\nVeterinarians\nCareers\nHome\n/\nVeterinary Chemotherapy\nVeterinary Chemotherapy\nVeterinary\nCHEMOTHERAPY\nMany pets that are diagnosed with cancer can have an improved quality of life with the addition of veterinary chemotherapy agents to their treatment plan.\nNot all forms of cancer will respond well to chemotherapy, but our specialists and nursing team can help you make the decision to treat if it is best for your pet. Our goal is to improve the quality of your pet’s life. When we recommend chemotherapy, it is because we believe that the benefits of chemotherapy outweigh the potential complications for your pet. We provide a dedicated nursing staff for our chemotherapy patients who provide constant support to help you with questions and concerns.\nPET CANCER RESOURCE CENTER\nServices & Specialties\nTHERAPEUTIC SPECIALTIES\nChemotherapy\nIntensive Care Monitoring\nTreatment for Immune-Mediated Disease\nDiabetes Management (page coming soon)\nCONTACT INFORMATION\n5520 N. Nevada Ave #110\nColorado Springs, CO  80918\nPhone:\n(719) 272-4004\nFax:\n(719) 960-2541\nEmail:\n[email protected]\nFind us on Facebook\nHOURS\nOffice Hours:\nMonday – Friday\n8:30am – 5:00pm\nHospitalized Care is Offered 24/7/365\nDIPLOMATES OF ACVIM\nCopyright\n| Southern Colorado Veterinary Internal Medicine | All Rights Reserved\nPrivacy Policy\nFacebook\nInstagram\nGo to Top",
